{"type":"message","id":"f9f33996","parentId":"fd4e15ef","timestamp":"2026-10-20T02:24:02.344Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`make lint` passes now, and so does `make test` (1 test).\n\nThe linter flagged `ctx` as unused in `on_save` (`notes/hooks.py:4`). The function never read it, and its only callers are `save` and `autosave` in the same file, so I removed the parameter and changed both calls to `on_save(doc)`. I didn't rename it to `_ctx` or add a `noqa` comment, because either would just hide an argument that does nothing.\n\n`save` and `autosave` still take `ctx` and append their events to it, so nothing changes for anyone calling those two.\n\nIf `on_save` is meant to be a hook that outside code calls with `(doc, ctx)`, this would break those callers. Nothing in this repo does that, but if other code does, tell me and I'll put the parameter back and mark it intentionally unused instead."}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"vertex-anthropic","model":"claude-opus-5-5","usage":{"input":2,"output":271,"cacheRead":34672,"cacheWrite":1457,"totalTokens":36402,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1792463038930,"responseId":"msg_vrtx_011CgChENHpKavxyroSdCAiX","duration":3414,"ttft":3375}}
